  "_calibration": "Defaults were calibrated on Physics a54a3ef (Release, dt=7200 s): each limit is 3-10x the measured value so genuine regressions trip it while run-to-run noise does not. Measured: kepler_circular pos 4.5e-6 / energy 1e-12; kepler_eccentric(e=0.6) pos 2.8e-4 / energy 1.5e-5; planetary pos 7.8e-6 / vel 6.8e-4; conservation energy 1.1e-5, momentum 8e-16; reversibility 1e-16; padding 1.8e-9; convergence order 2.000. Time step checks calibrated on Physics 83f9883 + sub-stepping (Release): ui_scales pos 4.4e-5 / energy 6.9e-13 over 10 years, one update per scale from 1 h to 1 decade; changes_mid_run pos 1.7e-5 / energy 1.1e-6; split_invariance 0 (bitwise). convergence_order dt_levels are kept at or below the 7200 s maximum sub-step: larger frames are split into identical sub-steps, so their error no longer depends on dt. timestep_satellite (Sun-Earth-Moon, 20 updates of one year) measured moon 2.2e-1 / planet 8.8e-5: the moon limit is a target (1% of the lunar orbit after 20 years), not a calibration, so the check is not required and reports WARN until the integrator is improved; the planet limit is 3x the measured value."
